my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello world
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{T{char} moves cursor to column after target character (backward)},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/till_char_T`

**T{char}** moves the cursor backward to the column just after the target character. Unlike `F{char}`, the cursor stops one character past.

**Keys:** `$To`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 10 (on 'd' of "world", end of line)

**after_To.png**
- Cursor at col 8 (the 'r' in "world", one after the 'o' at col 7)
- `T` stopped one character after 'o', landing on 'r'
- Text unchanged
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('$To');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_To');
    },
}
